# Prefer dw-flow

## Start

Run `dw-flow` for work that builds or ships something. When this turn has used no skill, the request is the start of `dw-flow`.

A `dw-*` skill the user names still runs. *Done when:* the turn is inside `dw-flow`, or inside the skill the user named.

| Excuse | Reality |
|---|---|
| "This is a small edit, so the flow can wait" | A request with no skill is the start of `dw-flow`. The flow's own gates decide what to skip. |
| "I'll call the user-invoked skill myself" | `disable-model-invocation: true` makes that call a silent no-op. Name the slash command and let the user run it. |

## Direction change

When the user changes the direction of a `dw-*` skill already in progress:

1. Walk the `dw-flow` steps internally and write down the new ask and the desired output. *Done when:* that reading is one short paragraph.
2. Verify the paragraph with the user. *Done when:* the user has confirmed it or corrected it.
3. Grill with `dw-grilling` when a decision is still open. *Done when:* every open decision is resolved, or there was none.
4. Get approval on the next steps when no decision is open. *Done when:* the user has approved the next steps.

## Skills in this plugin

This table is the closed set of skills that ship in this plugin. A skill present in the session and absent from the table still counts: survey it the same way.

The agent may run a skill in the **agent** column. A skill in the **you** column is user-invoked. Suggest it by its slash command when it matches the ask, and do not call it.

| Skill | Who runs it | Suggest when the user is |
|---|---|---|
| `dw-flow` | agent | building or shipping, or no skill has run |
| `dw-pr-ready` | agent | keeping one PR merge-ready |
| `dw-review-prs` | agent | working the PRs waiting on them |
| `dw-knowledge` | agent | asking how a workflow is run here, or asking to remember one |
| `dw-handoff` | agent | asking for a handoff |
| `dw-grilling` | agent | leaving a plan decision open |
| `dw-git-ops` | agent | committing, pushing, branching, or opening a PR |
| `dw-deslop` | agent | asking to strip AI slop from the diff |
| `dw-runbook` | agent | asking to cache or rerun a shell workflow |
| `dw-env` | agent | cloning, bootstrapping, or checking the machine |
| `dw-post-merge-verification` | agent | asking whether a merged PR changed prod |
| `dw-continue` | you — `/dw-continue` | resuming a handoff already written |
| `dw-skill-authoring` | you — `/dw-skill-authoring` | writing, reviewing, or debugging a skill |
| `dw-ticket-manager` | you — `/dw-ticket-manager` | running an accepted set of settled tickets to draft PRs |

*Done when:* every row that matches the ask was either run (agent) or named to the user with its slash command (you), and no user-invoked skill was called.
